{% doc %}
  Renders a section/block image with a three-step fallback:
  1. the merchant-picked image (image_picker),
  2. a named draft asset from the theme's assets (Figma export crops used
     while the design is in draft/approval),
  3. a neutral placeholder block.

  @param {object} [image] - image_picker value
  @param {string} [draft_asset] - asset filename, e.g. "figma-hero-left.jpg"
  @param {string} img_class - class for the <img> (and placeholder <div>)
  @param {string} [sizes] - responsive sizes attribute for the picked image
  @param {string} [alt] - alt text
  @param {string} [loading] - "lazy" (default) or "eager"
  @param {number} [asset_width] - intrinsic width of the draft asset (default 756)
  @param {number} [asset_height] - intrinsic height of the draft asset (default 957)
  @example
  {% render 'draft-image', image: block.settings.image, draft_asset: block.settings.draft_asset, img_class: 'image-card__media', alt: block.settings.label %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign load = loading | default: 'lazy'
  assign alt_text = alt | default: ''
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  The ladder reaches 2400 because these are the full-bleed home cards: a
  half-viewport card on a 1920 retina screen already wants ~1920 real pixels,
  and a third-of-viewport one on a 5K screen wants ~1700. A 1600 ceiling left
  both of those short. Small candidates are all still here, so a phone keeps
  downloading a small file.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if image -%}
  {{-
    image
    | image_url: width: 3000
    | image_tag:
      widths: '600, 900, 1200, 1600, 2000, 2400, 3000',
      sizes: sizes,
      class: img_class,
      alt: alt_text,
      loading: load
  -}}
{%- elsif draft_asset != blank -%}
  <img
    src="{{ draft_asset | asset_url }}"
    class="{{ img_class }}"
    alt="{{ alt_text }}"
    loading="{{ load }}"
    width="{{ asset_width | default: 756 }}"
    height="{{ asset_height | default: 957 }}"
  >
{%- else -%}
  <div class="{{ img_class }} {{ img_class }}--placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></div>
{%- endif -%}
